  OUTCOME: the Jacobian of (force, vacuum) w.r.t. (lambda, C) is block triangular with rank 2 on the MU family;
           rank 1 iff dF/dlambda = 0.  The observed vacuum energy compensates C(lambda) for every lambda:
           kappa = 1/lambda is fixed only by the deep-slope identity a0 = s/lambda (adoption at lambda = 2),
           never by the vacuum datum.  Setting C(lambda) to produce kappa = 1/2 is calibration (control passed,
           genuinely capable of failing: a principle fixing C absolutely would flip it; the available one is
           ill-posed for this family and sign-wrong for the corpus saturating carriers).
